      insight: 'The EMPIRICAL test: if the effect inherently pre-exists in the cause-combination (v.1\'s position), we should be able to PERCEIVE it there before it arises. But we don\'t — we can\'t taste the cake in the raw batter. The pre-existence claim fails empirically, not just logically.',
